            <ArticleTitle>Adjunctive medical therapy for acute coronary syndromes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adjunctive therapy is critical in treating acute coronary syndromes. Aspirin, nitrates, beta-blockers, ACE inhibitors, HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors (statins), and intra-aortic balloon pumps all have important roles and should be considered on a case-by-case basis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
